{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/84949-embed-strobe-light-effect","id":84949,"title":"Embed: Strobe Light Effect","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-03-05T17:32:49-08:00","id":84949,"title":"Embed: Strobe Light Effect","content":"Hello there all, Korogra here. I am running a Demon game for a couple players and have been designing Embeds for it and decided to put one them up here for your viewing pleasure. Let me know what you guys think of it!<br /> <br /> Strobe Light Effect<br /> <br /> Have you ever noticed how people seem to move more slowly when lit with strobing and flashing lights? Stroboscopic effects can make objects to appear to slow down, stop, or even reverse in motion depending on the frequency and intensity of the light. With this Embed the Demon can make use of such phenomena, utilizing the lights around him to escape harm while his foes are left none the wiser.<br /> <br /> Athletics + Subterfuge<br /> <br /> action: Reflexive<br /> <br /> Dramatic Failure: not only does the power fail to function, but the demon is even more injured by the following attack, suffering an additional number of health levels of damage equal to Primium.<br /> <br /> Failure: the power simply fails to function.<br /> <br /> Success: when successfully activated reflexively during his turn, the demon is able to avoid an attack from a single source the following turn, even from sources that ordinarily ignore defense such as firearms or explosions. The lights within the demon's Primium rating in yards flash for a split moment during the turn following, making it appear as if the demon was successfully attacked when in reality he is completely unharmed as he was able to avoid the attack at just the right moment. As stated before that upon success this embed allows the demon to avoid damage from a single source in a turn, other opponents or environmental effects may affect him as normal. In addition, the demon must be lit by artificial lighting. The Embed does not function within natural light such as from the sun, moon, fire, etc.<br /> <br /> Exceptional Success: The demon may avoid damage from two sources that turn.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-05T19:43:49-08:00","id":85007,"title":"","content":"Two quick thoughts<br /> <br /> First it should work with fires, the actual effect does and it limits usefulness (doubly so in past settings)<br /> Second having the light in Primium yards flash is redundant or at worst limiting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/252-basketcase","name":"basketcase","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar252_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-06T11:43:26-08:00","id":85488,"title":"","content":"It also breaks the mold of other embeds were its a finesse attribute + relevant skill. Might I suggest Manipulation + Subterfuge for this one? That or turn it into a Interlock perhaps one using Check Backdrop and Ellipses, make the activation roll Dexterity + Athletics + Primum<br /> <br /> Also what class of embed is it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/991-pgolasze13","name":"pgolasze13","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-09T16:37:30-07:00","id":87801,"title":"","content":"Going by the feel, I'd call it cacophony. I'd also say make the pool Manipulation + Subterfuge and the radius Primum x 10 yards/meters, affecting any light source that is not the sun, moon, or stars.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1424-ghanjrho","name":"GhanjRho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1424_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"126"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}